WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.150 --> 00:00:03.575
The last decision is the biggest: leaving the boat.

2
00:00:03.825 --> 00:00:06.725
Abandon her only when she’s clearly lost.

3
00:00:06.975 --> 00:00:13.700
Even a swamped, capsized boat is far easier for a helicopter to find than a head in the water.

4
00:00:13.950 --> 00:00:21.100
Before you go, call for help every way you have: Mayday by voice, the DSC distress button, and the EPIRB.

5
00:00:21.350 --> 00:00:29.725
Life jackets on everyone, and take the grab bag: handheld radio, personal locator beacon, flares, water, medications.

6
00:00:29.975 --> 00:00:33.450
There’s an old saying: step up into the life raft.

7
00:00:33.700 --> 00:00:35.300
What does it mean?

8
00:00:36.300 --> 00:00:39.775
Leave only when the boat is sinking out from under you.

9
00:00:40.025 --> 00:00:43.500
If you have to climb down into the raft, it’s too soon.

10
00:00:43.750 --> 00:00:47.150
And stay together, near the boat’s last position.

11
00:00:47.400 --> 00:00:49.650
That’s where the search will start.

12
00:00:49.900 --> 00:00:51.875
That’s lesson eleven.

13
00:00:52.125 --> 00:00:54.000
Shout, point, throw.

14
00:00:54.250 --> 00:00:57.975
Williamson: sixty degrees, then reverse the rudder.

15
00:00:58.225 --> 00:01:00.275
Recover over the side.

16
00:01:00.525 --> 00:01:02.350
One, ten, one.

17
00:01:02.600 --> 00:01:04.650
And step up into the raft.

18
00:01:04.900 --> 00:01:07.225
Next time: calling for help.
